---
// Issue #782: /signin route alias → /signup (the portal's canonical auth page).
//
// The portal login link points to /signin, but historically that route returned
// 404. The canonical auth page is /signup, so we alias /signin to it.
//
// Why a meta-refresh page instead of `Astro.redirect()`:
//   The portal is built with `output: 'static'` (see astro.config.mjs) and served
//   by nginx via `try_files $uri $uri/ $uri.html =404`. In static output there is
//   no server round-trip, so `Astro.redirect()` (an SSR-only API) cannot be used.
//   Instead we ship a tiny self-contained HTML page. nginx serves it at /signin
//   (resolving /signin → /signin.html), returning 200; the browser is then sent to
//   /signup via an HTTP-equivalent meta refresh, with a JS fallback and a noscript
//   link so the redirect works with scripting disabled.
const SIGNIN_TARGET = '/signup';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <!-- Equivalent to a 302: send the client to the canonical auth page. -->
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content={`0; url=${SIGNIN_TARGET}`} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={SIGNIN_TARGET} />
    <title>Redirecting to sign in…</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>
      Redirecting to <a href={SIGNIN_TARGET}>sign in</a>…
    </p>
    <script is:inline>
      // Preferred redirect: replaces history entry so /signin doesn't linger.
      window.location.replace('/signup');
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
